"help.start.intro" = "Lumen keeps profiles: each is a browser of its own, with its own cookies, its own way out to the network and its own look to websites. Stopped profiles are encrypted with the master password.";
"help.start.first" = "First steps";
"help.start.step.new" = "Click New Profile (⌘N), name the profile and, if it needs one, give it a proxy.";
"help.start.step.launch" = "Choose the profile in the list and click Launch: its window opens.";
"help.start.step.proxies" = "Proxies are in Proxies on the left: they are added, checked and given to profiles there. Add takes an HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy, a VLESS, VMess, Trojan or Shadowsocks link, an OpenVPN connection from a .ovpn file, or a whole list.";
"help.start.step.lock" = "Lock, at the bottom left, stops all profiles, encrypts their data and forgets the keys, until the master password is typed again.";
"help.start.where" = "Where things are";
"help.start.where.palette" = "Commands and Search on the left, or ⌘K, is the command palette: any profile, action or section of Settings by its first letters.";
"help.start.where.scenarios" = "Scenarios on the left, or ⇧⌘E, is automation: steps Lumen takes in a profile for you. They can be recorded from what you do and run on a schedule.";
"help.start.where.api" = "Automation API on the left lets your scripts on this Mac drive the profiles, Selenium (WebDriver) among them.";
"help.start.where.more" = "The ⋯ button above the list: importing a profile, sync, the network guard, changing the master password.";
"help.start.where.settings" = "Settings: ⌘, or the gear at the bottom left.";
"help.start.where.check" = "Check the profile, in the profile panel on the right and in a profile's ⋯ menu: compares what sites see with where the profile exits to the internet.";
"help.start.where.codes" = "A profile's Passwords and Codes: its saved passwords and, beside them, the one-time codes of two-step sign-in.";
"help.palette.intro" = "The command palette is the shortest way to anything in Lumen. Open it with ⌘K, or with Commands and Search on the left of the Profiles window, and start typing.";
"help.palette.finds" = "What it finds";
"help.palette.finds.profiles" = "Profiles, by name, tags and where they exit: launch, stop, open a new window, edit, warm up, check, open passwords and codes.";
"help.palette.finds.actions" = "Actions: a new profile, the proxies, the warm-up queue, sync, Lock, the scenarios, the automation API, Help.";
"help.palette.finds.settings" = "The sections of Settings, by name.";
"help.palette.finds.report" = "Copy Short Report: the diagnostics as one text, on the clipboard.";
"help.palette.keys" = "Keys";
"help.palette.key.choose" = "Choose a row";
"help.palette.key.run" = "Run the chosen one";
"help.palette.key.close" = "Close the palette";
"help.scenarios.intro" = "A scenario does in a profile what a person would: goes to pages, clicks, types, waits. Lumen moves the pointer and presses the keys itself, with no debugging protocol: a page gets mouse and keyboard events. A scenario is made from a template, recorded from what you do, or written in JavaScript — and reads as steps either way.";
"help.scenarios.plan" = "Running and recording scenarios, and schedules, are part of the Professional and Team plans, and of the trial. On Personal, scenarios can be written, not run.";
"help.scenarios.how" = "How to run a scenario";
"help.scenarios.step.open" = "Open Scenarios: on the left of the Profiles window, in the File menu, or with ⇧⌘E.";
"help.scenarios.step.new" = "In Templates choose one — its steps and what it asks for are shown beside the list — press Use the Template and answer its questions. Or New Scenario › Record Actions, or Start with Example Code.";
"help.scenarios.step.write" = "The scenario opens as its settings and steps beside its code. Click a step to change it, move it, switch it off or delete it; the code is always what is true. ⌘S saves.";
"help.scenarios.step.run" = "Check runs it once on the profile chosen under the name and marks the step that failed. Run… (⌘R) takes many profiles: by search or by tag, so many at once. Lumen starts stopped profiles itself.";
"help.scenarios.step.log" = "The run's table says for each profile whether it is done, which step failed and why, how long it took and what the scenario returned. Click a row for its steps and its log. Run the Failed Again runs only those. The last 100 runs are kept under Runs.";
"help.scenarios.example" = "An example: signing in";
"help.scenarios.example.code" = "await page.goto('https://shop.example/login');\nawait page.type('#email', 'name@example.com');\nawait page.type('#password', 'your password');\nawait page.press('Enter');\nawait page.waitFor('text=My orders');\nlog('Signed in:', await page.title());";
"help.scenarios.know" = "Worth knowing";
"help.scenarios.know.window" = "A scenario runs in a window of Safari’s that Lumen opens for the run: the profile’s real window, with its cookies and proxy. A profile seen as an iPhone or iPad has no Safari window: its scenario runs in Lumen’s own.";
"help.scenarios.know.await" = "Every command of page waits for the page and returns a promise: write await before it.";
"help.scenarios.know.errors" = "A command that fails throws an error with the reason and the line of the scenario it was on. try and catch can catch it; one left uncaught ends the run.";
"help.scenarios.know.typed" = "The log says how many characters were typed, never which: no password is in it.";
"help.scenarios.know.kept" = "Scenarios, a profile's values and the runs are kept in the vault on this Mac, encrypted. They are not synced. A scenario can be exported to a file and imported on another Mac; a profile's values never go into the file.";
"help.scenarios.record" = "Recording a scenario";
"help.scenarios.record.text" = "A scenario need not be written by hand. Choose a profile and press Record, then do in the profile's window what is to be repeated. Each page opened, click and typing appears as a line; Stop Recording adds them to the scenario's end, where they can be changed. In a new scenario that still holds the example, what was recorded takes its place.";
"help.scenarios.record.selectors" = "Elements are found by what lasts: an id, a name, data-testid, a label, a button's text — and only when there is none of these, by their place on the page.";
"help.scenarios.record.password" = "What is typed into a password’s field — or a one-time code’s, or a card’s — is not recorded: the line has params.password. Give the profile its own value named password (Scenarios window, the profile’s values), write the password in its place, or pass it as a parameter when the run is started through the API.";
"help.scenarios.record.limits" = "What is recorded is what is done on the page itself. A choice in a drop-down list is recorded as page.selectOption; a card’s month or year, and a list that takes several choices, as a comment. Dragging, file uploads and embedded frames are not recorded.";
"help.scenarios.schedule" = "Schedule";
"help.scenarios.schedule.text" = "Schedule is a tab of Scenarios, and On a Schedule… in a scenario's ⋯ menu opens it. A scenario, or a profile's warm-up, runs every day at a time or every so many hours, with a random shift either way.";
"help.scenarios.schedule.running" = "A schedule runs while Lumen is open and the vault is unlocked: it does not wake the Mac or start the app. A run missed by more than 6 hours is not made; it waits for the next time. If the profile is busy then, the run moves on by 10 minutes. The schedule says how its last run ended: finished and in how long, or failed and why.";
"help.commands.intro" = "The commands belong to page. A selector is CSS (#login, .buy, input[name=q]) or text=…, the smallest visible element holding that text; login-box >>> input[name=email] looks inside a page component (its open shadow root). Options go last, in braces, such as {timeout: 30000}, in milliseconds.";
"help.commands.navigation" = "Going to pages";
"help.commands.goto" = "Goes to an http or https address, as the address bar does, and waits for the page. {waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded'} does not wait for pictures and styles.";
"help.commands.history" = "Back, forward, reload, as the toolbar’s buttons; they wait for the page.";
"help.commands.loadState" = "Waits for the page’s state: 'load' or 'domcontentloaded'. Right after a click, a key or a choice in a list it first waits for the page that opens, so the old page is not read by mistake.";
"help.commands.waiting" = "Waiting";
"help.commands.waitFor" = "Waits for an element. {state: 'visible'} by default; also 'hidden', 'attached', 'detached'. Not there within the timeout is an error.";
"help.commands.waitForURL" = "Waits until the page’s address matches, then for the page: '**/account' (* is a run of characters within one part of the path, ** any run) or a regular expression, /\\/orders\\/\\d+$/. For a page that comes late after a click.";
"help.commands.sleep" = "A pause, in milliseconds. sleep(Infinity) waits until the run is stopped.";
"help.commands.acting" = "Acting";
"help.commands.click" = "Waits for the element, scrolls it into view with the wheel, moves the pointer onto it and clicks. An element covered by another is an error naming what covers it.";
"help.commands.dblclick" = "A double click. The same as page.click(selector, {clickCount: 2}).";
"help.commands.hover" = "Moves the pointer onto the element.";
"help.commands.selectOption" = "Chooses in a drop-down list: an option’s value or its words, {label: …}, {value: …} or {index: 2}; a list of them where the list takes several. The pointer goes to the list; the choice itself is set by Lumen, as AutoFill sets a field, so the page’s input and change events are not marked as a person’s.";
"help.commands.type" = "Clicks the field and types the text key by key. {delay: 120} is the pause between keys, about that many milliseconds.";
"help.commands.press" = "A key or a combination: 'Tab', 'Shift+Tab', 'Meta+a'. The keys with names: Enter, Tab, Backspace, Delete, Escape, Space, ArrowLeft, ArrowRight, ArrowUp, ArrowDown, Home, End, PageUp, PageDown.";
"help.commands.scroll" = "Scrolls with the wheel that many points down; a negative number scrolls up.";
"help.commands.reading" = "Reading the page";
"help.commands.text" = "The element’s text.";
"help.commands.inputValue" = "What a field holds.";
"help.commands.getAttribute" = "An attribute’s value, href for one.";
"help.commands.count" = "How many elements the selector finds.";
"help.commands.isVisible" = "Whether the element shows: true or false.";
"help.commands.url" = "The page’s address and title.";
"help.commands.evaluate" = "Runs a function on the page and gives its result. It runs in a world of its own, which the page’s scripts cannot see.";
"help.commands.screenshot" = "A picture of the part of the page in view, or of an element with page.screenshot(selector). The result is a PNG in base64.";
"help.commands.script" = "In the scenario itself";
"help.commands.log" = "A line in the run’s log.";
"help.commands.params" = "The run’s parameters: the profile’s own values for scenarios (Scenarios window, the profile’s values) that the scenario’s text names as params.name or params['name'], so that one scenario has each profile’s login and password; and what a request of the automation API gives in params, which wins.";
"help.commands.result" = "What the scenario returns is the run’s result: shown in the log, and given as result by the automation API.";
"help.api.intro" = "A script on this Mac can do what the Profiles window does: list the profiles, start and stop one, open a page in it, read and write its cookies, run a scenario. It connects only from this Mac (127.0.0.1) and only with the token.";
"help.api.plan" = "The API is part of the Professional and Team plans, and of the trial. Without it every request is refused with 403 automation_not_in_plan.";
"help.api.on" = "Turning it on";
"help.api.step.open" = "Open Automation API on the left of the Profiles window, or the section of that name in Settings.";
"help.api.step.enable" = "Turn on “Let scripts on this Mac drive the profiles”.";
"help.api.step.token" = "Copy the token. The port is 50777 unless you change it there.";
"help.api.step.unlocked" = "The API answers while the vault is unlocked.";
"help.api.try" = "Trying it in Terminal";
"help.api.try.code" = "export PB_API_TOKEN='the token from Automation API'\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PB_API_TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:50777/v1/profiles";
"help.api.requests" = "Requests";
"help.api.request.list" = "Every profile.";
"help.api.request.one" = "One profile. {profile} is its id or its exact name, encoded for an address. A name two profiles share is refused: use the id.";
"help.api.request.start" = "Starts it. The body {\"window\": false} starts it without a window. A running profile is left as it is.";
"help.api.request.stop" = "Stops it. The profile’s data is encrypted before the answer comes.";
"help.api.request.open" = "A new window of the running profile at the body’s address: {\"url\": \"https://…\"}.";
"help.api.request.cookies" = "Every cookie of the profile. ?format=playwright (the default), netscape or extension.";
"help.api.request.importCookies" = "Imports the cookies in the body: a JSON or a Netscape file.";
"help.api.request.scenario" = "Runs a scenario on the running profile: {\"source\": \"…\", \"params\": {…}}, or a saved one, {\"scenario\": \"Its name\"}. A saved scenario also has in params the profile’s own values that its text names.";
"help.api.request.scenarioState" = "The profile’s last run: whether it is running, how it ended, its log, and its result — what the scenario returned.";
"help.api.request.scenarioStop" = "Stops the run: a wait under way ends, a pressed button or key is let go.";
"help.api.scenario" = "A scenario from a script";
"help.api.scenario.code" = "curl -s -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $PB_API_TOKEN\" -d '{\"source\": \"await page.goto(params.url); log(await page.title());\", \"params\": {\"url\": \"https://example.com/\"}}' http://127.0.0.1:50777/v1/profiles/Shop/scenario";
"help.api.errors" = "Errors";
"help.api.errors.text" = "An error comes as {\"error\": \"code\", \"message\": \"text\"}. 401: no token, or a wrong one. 403 automation_not_in_plan: the plan has no automation. 404: no such profile. 409: two profiles share the name (ambiguous), the profile is not running (not_running) or is busy (busy).";
"help.api.token" = "Whoever has the token can start your profiles and read their cookies. Show it to no one; New Token, in the same window, ends the old one at once.";
"help.api.webdriver" = "Selenium and WebDriver";
"help.api.webdriver.text" = "Your own Selenium scripts run on a Lumen profile as they do on Safari: Lumen answers the standard W3C WebDriver protocol. The system's safaridriver cannot be used for it: it drives Safari itself only.";
"help.api.webdriver.step.on" = "Turn the automation API on: Automation API on the left of the Profiles window, or the section of that name in Settings.";
"help.api.webdriver.step.copy" = "Select the profile and copy WebDriver Address in the profile panel on the right — or choose Copy WebDriver Address in the profile's ⋯ menu.";
"help.api.webdriver.step.script" = "Give the address to the script as command_executor.";
"help.api.webdriver.code" = "from selenium import webdriver\nfrom selenium.webdriver.common.by import By\n\n# The address is in the profile panel: WebDriver Address → Copy\ndriver = webdriver.Remote(\n    command_executor='http://127.0.0.1:50777/wd/<token>/<profile>',\n    options=webdriver.SafariOptions())\n\ndriver.get('https://example.com/')\ndriver.find_element(By.CSS_SELECTOR, 'input[name=q]').send_keys('lumen')\ndriver.find_element(By.XPATH, '//button[@type=\"submit\"]').click()\nprint(driver.title)\ndriver.quit()  # closes the window; a profile the session started is stopped";
"help.api.webdriver.session" = "A new session starts the profile if it is stopped and opens a Safari window of its own for its commands: a scenario never runs in it. quit closes the window, and stops the profile only if the session started it; a profile that was running, out of sight too, stays. A profile has one session at a time, and while it lasts a scheduled scenario of the profile waits.";
"help.api.webdriver.human" = "Clicks and typing are the scenarios': the pointer travels to the element, the keys are pressed one by one. The page takes them for a person's, and navigator.webdriver stays false.";
"help.api.webdriver.scripts" = "execute_script runs in a world of its own in the page: the DOM, elements as arguments and elements returned work; the page's own variables (window.app and the like) are not seen from it.";
"help.api.webdriver.limits" = "There is: navigation, finding by CSS and XPath, click, send_keys (with Keys.HOME, END, PAGE_DOWN, DELETE), clear, text and attributes, execute_script, cookies, a screenshot, the window's size, waits, and ActionChains for a hover (move_to_element), click, double_click, keys, the wheel and pauses. There is not: frames, alert dialogs, several tabs, file uploads, and of ActionChains a drag, the right button and a click with a modifier key held.";
"help.api.webdriver.playwright" = "Playwright cannot be connected: it drives only its own builds of browsers and does not speak WebDriver. Its script moves into a Lumen scenario almost word for word — page.goto, page.click, page.type have the same names.";
"help.api.webdriver.see" = "Your Selenium scripts connect to a profile over WebDriver, on the same port, with a token of the profile's own made from the API's. How: the Selenium and WebDriver topic on the left.";
"help.keys.app" = "In Lumen’s windows";
"help.keys.palette" = "The command palette";
