"vm.base.guide" = "# What to press in macOS's setup\nLanguage and country: any.\nInternet connection: any — \"My computer does not connect to the Internet\" or a cable. The machines do not depend on it.\nTransfer information: \"Not Now\".\n! Apple ID: \"Set Up Later\", then \"Skip\". Do not sign in: the Apple ID would be in every machine.\nTerms: \"Agree\".\nAccount: any name; a new password made up for this machine only, not your Mac's.\nLocation, analytics, Screen Time, Siri: off, or \"Set Up Later\".\n! FileVault: do not turn it on — with it the machines cannot sign in by themselves.\nAppearance: any.\n! At the desktop: Finder → Go → Computer → \"My Shared Files\" → \"Install Lumen Tools\", and type this account's password. The machine shuts down by itself, and that is all.\n> Chose something else? \"Install Lumen Tools\" checks, and says what to change.\n> If a double-click does not start it: Terminal → sh \"/Volumes/My Shared Files/install.sh\"";
